Skip non-UPnP services instead of rejecting the whole device.

pa-dlna parses every service listed in a device description and fetches its
SCPD, expecting the `urn:schemas-upnp-org:` namespace. The Bose SoundTouch
advertises a Tencent "QPlay" service whose SCPD uses
`urn:schemas-tencent-com:service-1-0`, so upnp_org_etree() raises
UPnPXMLError('No namespace starting with urn:schemas-upnp-org:') and the entire
MediaRenderer (AVTransport/RenderingControl/ConnectionManager) is discarded —
no sink is ever created. Skip services whose serviceType is not in the UPnP
namespace; pa-dlna doesn't use QPlay anyway.

Upstream: https://gitlab.com/xdegaye/pa-dlna
--- a/pa_dlna/upnp/upnp.py
+++ b/pa_dlna/upnp/upnp.py
@@ -308,6 +308,13 @@
             if 'serviceId' not in d:
                 raise UPnPXMLError("Missing 'serviceId' element")

+            # Skip non-UPnP services (e.g. the Tencent 'QPlay' service the
+            # Bose SoundTouch advertises) whose SCPD uses a non-upnp
+            # namespace and would otherwise make upnp_org_etree() reject
+            # the whole device.
+            if not d.get('serviceType', '').startswith(
+                    'urn:schemas-upnp-org:'):
+                continue
             serviceId = d['serviceId']
             self.serviceList[serviceId] = await (
                                 UPnPService(self, self.root_device, d)._run())
